    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **James Wood** serving as our clear focal point. Boasting an elite 78.42 score, **Wood** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Chandler, where his .420 xwOBA and top-tier order placement set the stage for an explosive offensive contribution. Alongside him, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Brice Turang** (73.40) offer the high-floor efficiency we crave. **Moniak** is a primary beneficiary of a massive 14% platoon edge against Mahle in a hitter-friendly environment, while **Turang** continues to be a priority play due to his leadoff role and the 19% boost derived from a favorable matchup against a vulnerable rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's bench involved **Cole Young**, who landed just outside our starting nine with a 49.98 score. While **Young** offers utility value, the current configuration prioritized the higher upside of **Max Muncy** and **Alex Freeland**, the latter of whom draws a significant 19% advantage against Sears. We are keeping a close eye on the wind conditions favoring **Freeland**, which could see his output outperform the current projection. Conversely, we are exercising caution with **Corbin Carroll** (73.03); despite his elite speed, the presence of an elite catcher behind the plate mandates a slight downward adjustment to our stolen base expectations. We will continue to monitor the status of **Austin Riley** and **Travis Bazzana** on our bench, as their current efficiency scores suggest they are ready to rotate in should any of our starters face late-scratches or lineup volatility.",
